{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BGD47wSsxjBb1bfq855eLo","type":"tool_result","content":"79:\\caption{Solver comparison on Qwen2.5-7B at $4\\times$ compression. Unconstrained solvers over-allocate 2-bit heads and fail catastrophically. The cardinality constraint ($k{\\leq}8$) makes greedy and MCKP produce identical allocations.\\protect\\footnotemark}\n94:\\footnotetext{Constrained results use high-resolution profiling; unconstrained rows use standard-resolution profiling to illustrate the failure mode (the exact PPL is irrelevant---any unconstrained allocation fails catastrophically).}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MG8RGMZBgpjvNJWxBwBHSt","session_id":"f6b0b3c4-17a1-4fb2-92fd-0f4f71a4e809","uuid":"e104b041-57ca-49cd-9cf2-0ba2c4818ea1","timestamp":"2026-05-16T02:55:02.991Z"}
